## Standalone Minimum Gate

This repository must remain usable without personal global Agent rules or optional global Skills:

1. Before editing, summarize the goal, in/out of scope, acceptance criteria, affected modules/files, and ambiguities/risks. Ask before editing when ambiguity changes behavior, contracts, data, permissions, billing, security, or workflow.
2. Inspect the existing Owner, similar implementations, reusable modules, dependency boundaries, test locations, generators, and verification commands. Do not add parallel logic without justification.
3. For bugs, reproduce or explain why reproduction is unavailable, add a regression test that would fail before the fix, then verify it passes. For features, cover the happy path, invalid input, edge cases, relevant permission/state boundaries, and nearby regressions. Add a permanent test only for observable behavior, a stable contract/invariant, a known regression, or a meaningful boundary with an independent expected result; do not test an internal method merely because it was added or duplicate stronger owner-level coverage.
4. Before delivery, report requirement match, design/reuse decisions, changed and generated files, commands and results, remaining risks, and rollback/recovery notes when relevant.

Optional global rules may provide stricter or more detailed guidance when installed; this section is the repository-local fallback, not a second full engineering standard.
